From: Sam Derbyshire <sam.derbyshire@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Carefully implement coercion zapping (GHC 10.0 backport)

Backport of f56f7c594bee4ca2d578c116fe684545c65e3dbf from GHC !16378:
https://gitlab.haskell.org/ghc/ghc/-/merge_requests/16378

Adapted to GHC 10.0.0.20260917's Core Lint API and UnivCoProvenance.
The release source archive omits testsuite/, so upstream tests are not
included in this build patch.

diff --git a/changelog.d/zap-coercions b/changelog.d/zap-coercions
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changelog.d/zap-coercions
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+section: compiler
+synopsis: Speed up type-family-heavy programs by zapping coercions
+issues: #8095 #27336 #27518
+mrs: !16378
+description: {
+  GHC now erases the coercions that it produces when reducing type family
+  applications, keeping only their endpoints and the assumptions they used
+  (a process called "zapping").
+  This greatly speeds up the compilation of type-family-heavy programs (#8095).
+
+  This behaviour is controlled by ``-fzap-coercions`` and enabled by default;
+  disable with ``-fno-zap-coercions``.
+}
